{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answer\":\"“Lua monitors” means Hyprland’s Lua-based monitor configuration, introduced as the preferred configuration format in Hyprland 0.55. The core form is `hl.monitor({ output = \\\"DP-1\\\", mode = \\\"1920x1080@144\\\", position = \\\"0x0\\\", scale = 1 })`; use `hyprctl monitors all` to discover output names and modes. In Omarchy, these rules normally live in `~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua`; an empty `output = \\\"\\\"` acts as a fallback for unspecified displays. Be careful with Omarchy’s current catch-all scale variable on multi-monitor systems: its Display panel may persist one monitor’s scale globally, so explicit per-output rules are safer when you need stable independent scales.\",\"sources\":[{\"title\":\"Hyprland Wiki — Monitors\",\"url\":\"https://wiki.hypr.land/0.55.0/Configuring/Basics/Monitors/\"},{\"title\":\"Hyprland official Lua example\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/hyprwm/Hyprland/blob/main/example/hyprland.lua\"},{\"title\":\"Omarchy monitor scaling issue\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/basecamp/omarchy/issues/6673\"}]}"}}
